# Mosquitto ACL for the ASIIS telemetry channel.
#
# Principle: every device may PUBLISH only under its own concrete topic
# prefix  {base}/{farm_id}/{its_code}/telemetry/...  and may never
# subscribe to other devices' topics. The backend subscriber account gets
# read access to the whole tree.
#
# NOTE: the password file and this ACL are the broker-side half of device
# auth; the ASIIS backend re-checks topic<->key binding per message
# (defence in depth, and the only enforcement that exists on the
# unauthenticated in-process fallback bus — see app/iot/bus.py docstring).

# Backend service account: subscribe everything, publish nothing.
user asiis-backend
topic read asiis/v1/#

# Device accounts: one write-pinned topic prefix per device, generated at
# registration (farm_id and code are known then). Add one block per device:
#
# user PROBE-1                       # username = device code
# topic write asiis/v1/7/PROBE-1/telemetry/soil
#
# user WX-1
# topic write asiis/v1/7/WX-1/telemetry/weather
